{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Judges and officers.</b> After the commandments addressed to the multitude, He commanded the matters of its leaders — kings, judges, priests, and prophets — through whose rectification the condition of the multitude is rectified, and through whose corruption it is corrupted, as the prophet admonished, saying: שָׂרֶיהָ בְקִרְבָּהּ אֲרָיוֹת שׁוֹאֲגִים, שֹׁפְטֶיהָ זְאֵבֵי עֶרֶב לֹא גָרְמוּ לַבֹּקֶר, נְבִיאֶיהָ פֹּחֲזִים אַנְשֵׁי בֹגְדוֹת, כֹּהֲנֶיהָ חִלְּלוּ קֹדֶשׁ חָמְסוּ תוֹרָה (Zephaniah 3:3–4)." "<b>Which He gives you, for your tribes.</b> In your gates — that is, what He gives you to divide among your tribes, not in what you conquer outside the Land, which is not divided among the tribes. As the Sages, of blessed memory, stated (Sanhedrin): בְּחוּצָה לָאָרֶץ אֵין אַתָּה מוֹשִׁיב דַּיָּנִים בְּכָל פֶּלֶךְ וּבְכָל עִיר וָעִיר, and this applies to Syria and the like." "<b>Righteous judgment.</b> The reception of pleadings is to be such that the judgment is decided in righteousness — that he be neither lenient to one nor harsh to the other."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:39.075294365Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}